WEBVTT

00:02.105 --> 00:04.190
Hello, Kawajiri residence.

00:02.439 --> 00:04.649
JULY 16TH (FRI) 7:57 AM

00:04.816 --> 00:07.151
Huh? I'm sorry,
you have the wrong number.

00:08.820 --> 00:10.780
Really… Superb job, Hayato.

00:11.573 --> 00:16.073
So you've kept that irksome
Rohan at bay.

00:17.245 --> 00:19.455
I said you've got the wrong number.

00:19.498 --> 00:20.499
Goodbye.

00:20.624 --> 00:22.584
- Misdialed call.
- Now, then…

00:22.751 --> 00:27.251
I have to provide for
my sweet, beautiful family.

00:30.592 --> 00:32.302
But first,
I wonder if a certain someone

00:32.344 --> 00:34.554
will allow me to give her
a goodbye kiss?

00:34.596 --> 00:35.638
Huh?

00:48.735 --> 00:51.988
What are you doing?!
My expensive china…

00:52.948 --> 00:55.158
Why would you do such a thing?!

00:55.283 --> 00:58.160
I never know what's going on
inside that head of yours!

00:58.245 --> 01:01.831
You act like you don't
even hear me! Why?!

01:02.958 --> 01:03.959
I just…

01:10.799 --> 01:14.469
<i>Mom, he's no ordinary person.</i>

01:14.636 --> 01:17.013
<i>If I so much as utter a word
about him to anyone,</i>

01:17.055 --> 01:18.222
<i>the listener will be
blown to smithereens,</i>

01:18.306 --> 01:19.682
<i>and time will reset to morning.</i>

01:20.350 --> 01:23.061
<i>If we keep letting him
have free reign overall our lives,</i>

01:23.270 --> 01:27.023
<i>maybe not now, but eventually,
we will die by his hands.</i>

01:42.372 --> 01:44.415
<i>R-Rohan Kishibe…</i>

01:44.499 --> 01:47.210
<i>But there is someone else
who has special powers like Kira.</i>

01:47.294 --> 01:49.713
<i>I've got to talk to
Rohan Kishibe somehow.</i>

01:49.754 --> 01:52.506
<i>The only one who can save us
and beat Kira</i>

01:52.549 --> 01:55.760
<i>is someone with special powers
like Rohan Kishibe!</i>

02:01.099 --> 02:03.142
<i>He's here. It's Rohan.</i>

02:03.852 --> 02:07.230
<i>If I approach Rohan directly,
he'll be killed by explosives…</i>

02:07.272 --> 02:10.275
<i>Then I'll be forced to
relive that same morning.</i>

02:10.358 --> 02:12.234
<i>I've got to figure out a way
to tell Rohan the info</i>

02:12.319 --> 02:13.695
<i>without meeting him face to face.</i>

02:14.487 --> 02:16.530
<i>It's time to alter destiny's plans!</i>

02:18.700 --> 02:22.787
FLIP

02:21.703 --> 02:24.247
<i>W-What's going on?!</i>

02:22.871 --> 02:27.333
[WARNING]
DO NOT READ ON.

02:24.372 --> 02:27.355
<i>It's what Rohan did to me
that morning from before!</i>

02:29.044 --> 02:30.295
Dammit.

02:33.214 --> 02:35.841
But I was hidden
from Rohan this time!

02:35.967 --> 02:38.427
Rohan didn't even see me!

02:38.762 --> 02:41.848
Once the wheels of fate
are set in motion,

02:41.890 --> 02:43.433
there's no turning back…

02:45.101 --> 02:46.644
Hayato.

02:48.396 --> 02:50.064
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

02:50.732 --> 02:52.859
<i>(Listen up)
Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

03:04.746 --> 03:06.456
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

03:07.582 --> 03:09.208
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

03:14.547 --> 03:19.047
<i>Let the voice of love
take you higher</i>

03:19.594 --> 03:24.094
<i>Let the gathering forces
overcome time itself</i>

03:27.310 --> 03:31.810
<i>Let the joy of love
give you an answer</i>

03:32.273 --> 03:36.773
<i>Our Willis unbreakable
even when it's time to part</i>

03:38.613 --> 03:43.113
<i>1999 Bizarre Summer</i>

03:43.576 --> 03:48.076
<i>This is the hymn born from
our fearless hearts</i>

03:52.043 --> 03:55.546
<i>Great Days
Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

03:55.630 --> 03:57.298
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

03:58.425 --> 04:00.051
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

04:01.261 --> 04:02.845
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

04:06.766 --> 04:08.517
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

04:09.019 --> 04:10.645
July 16th (Fri) 8:27 AM

04:12.147 --> 04:16.484
Ugh, the weather report
never said anything about rain.

04:12.439 --> 04:16.939
EPISODE 36
BITES THE DUST, PART 2

04:20.196 --> 04:24.696
You may think you broke that
teapot out of your own free will,

04:25.660 --> 04:26.827
but you'd be wrong.

04:27.037 --> 04:29.289
It's simply a re-occurrence
of the pot breaking

04:29.330 --> 04:31.248
from the previous morning.

04:32.333 --> 04:34.501
It's preordained.

04:35.462 --> 04:37.881
That is how fate works.

04:37.964 --> 04:40.883
If Rohan transformed your noggin
into a book the morning before,

04:40.925 --> 04:43.052
then it is a book you shall be.

04:43.428 --> 04:46.931
That, my boy, is what makes Deadly
Queen's Bites the Dust unstoppable.

04:47.140 --> 04:48.933
It makes the exposure
of my identity

04:49.017 --> 04:51.227
as if it never happened,
reversing time in the process.

04:52.729 --> 04:56.774
Which means I get to enjoy watching
Rohan explode into obsolescence

04:56.858 --> 04:59.443
before I jaunt off to work.

04:59.903 --> 05:03.406
IT RAINED.
AT 8:27 AM, LIGHTNING STRUCK
ABOVE THE PEPSI SIGN.

05:01.196 --> 05:03.427
<i>I can't let Rohan die!</i>

05:04.657 --> 05:07.409
<i>I have to save Rohan!</i>

05:23.510 --> 05:26.304
Ah, Rohan Kishibe.

05:27.555 --> 05:28.472
Now watch.

05:28.556 --> 05:32.935
He has no idea why
he's about to breathe his last.

05:34.270 --> 05:36.146
"My life as a manga artist is over…"

05:36.231 --> 05:38.816
Must be tearing through
his head right now.

05:58.920 --> 06:01.213
R-Rohan…

06:05.677 --> 06:08.262
No, god, please!

06:13.017 --> 06:17.479
Hayato, your visit with Rohan
is now as if it never happened,

06:17.564 --> 06:20.191
and the morning will go on
as it always would.

06:20.275 --> 06:22.610
Of course,
if I undo Bites the Dust now,

06:22.652 --> 06:26.781
Rohan's death will become
not temporary but ever lasting…

06:27.157 --> 06:29.492
But for now,
I'll let it do its thing.

06:29.534 --> 06:32.662
I expect a few of his friends
to come join the party.

06:33.830 --> 06:38.000
You will exterminate them
automatically for me.

06:38.793 --> 06:40.294
You're my own personal landmine.

06:42.422 --> 06:46.922
But Bites the Dust will leave you
completely unharmed,

06:47.468 --> 06:50.846
so relax, do whatever
you school boys do.

06:53.266 --> 06:55.101
Well, time for Dad
to head to the station.

06:55.143 --> 06:57.311
No slacking at school now.

07:01.316 --> 07:04.944
<i>It's my fault.
He crossed paths with me…</i>

07:05.236 --> 07:08.614
<i>He crossed paths with me
and was murdered!</i>

07:20.251 --> 07:24.751
<i>Isn't there something I can do
to defeat this monster?</i>

07:31.554 --> 07:34.515
Um… Pardon me,
but I have a question…

07:35.475 --> 07:37.393
You wouldn't happen to
have the time, would you?

07:37.977 --> 07:40.604
My watch seems to be out of whack.

07:41.189 --> 07:43.191
Hello? Anyone home?

07:46.861 --> 07:49.113
It's 8:33…

07:49.197 --> 07:52.575
Huh? I have this weird feeling
I've seen you somewhere before…

07:52.617 --> 07:54.160
Where was it?

07:54.619 --> 07:56.662
Do you know who I am?

07:57.288 --> 07:58.038
No…

07:58.039 --> 08:00.041
Oh, I guess it's all in my head.

08:00.291 --> 08:02.668
Sorry for
the off-the-wall question.

08:03.294 --> 08:06.255
8:33… Thanks!

08:07.423 --> 08:10.759
Mr. Jotaro! So it is after 8:30.

08:10.927 --> 08:14.472
Strange, I wonder where
Rohan-sensei went.

08:15.223 --> 08:17.516
<i>Rohan Kishibe's friends!</i>

08:17.600 --> 08:19.059
<i>They planned to meet here!</i>

08:19.352 --> 08:20.394
- He left the car door
<i>- They must have</i>

08:20.436 --> 08:21.979
- wide open
<i>- the same kind of powers…</i>

08:22.063 --> 08:23.189
- and the key in the ignition.
<i>- They're here to question me</i>

08:23.231 --> 08:26.359
- Rohan-sensei would never do that…
<i>- about Yoshikage Kira.</i>

08:33.074 --> 08:37.369
<i>No! If they figure out
I'm Hayato Kawajiri and start</i>

08:37.412 --> 08:39.997
<i>- interrogating me about Dad…</i>
- That's Rohan-Sensei's earring.

08:44.585 --> 08:46.420
Oops, sorry…

08:46.462 --> 08:49.173
I overslept and am supposed to
meet up with my friends.

08:49.257 --> 08:52.969
Hey… I've seen that face before…
Now where?

08:55.138 --> 08:57.306
Ah, Josuke and Okuyasu.

08:57.390 --> 08:58.140
Yo.

08:58.224 --> 09:01.268
Yo, Koichi.
Top of the morning to ya, Jotaro.

09:01.602 --> 09:04.354
<i>- A-And two more…</i>
- What, so the only one

09:04.439 --> 09:05.982
<i>- He said more of them</i>
- we're waiting for is Rohan?

09:06.065 --> 09:07.399
<i>Would be showing up…</i>

09:07.442 --> 09:09.777
<i>- He was talking about them!</i>
- How the hell are we supposed to

09:09.819 --> 09:11.612
find Hayato Kawajiri
without him here.

09:12.822 --> 09:15.491
Sorry, I forgot I was still
hanging on to this.

09:16.284 --> 09:18.369
Here. Your hat.

09:18.786 --> 09:21.205
Th-Thanks…

09:21.998 --> 09:24.375
When I look at his face
from this angle…

09:24.584 --> 09:28.462
That angle. I know I've seen
that face somewhere…

09:29.005 --> 09:32.717
But where?
Where have I seen that face…

09:32.842 --> 09:35.469
Koichi. Look at the name
on his backpack.

09:35.720 --> 09:36.720
Huh?

09:36.262 --> 09:38.681
HAYATO KAWAJIRI

09:37.138 --> 09:38.702
Hayato Kawajiri?!

09:38.973 --> 09:40.641
What?!

09:40.683 --> 09:42.935
<i>They figured me out!</i>

09:46.606 --> 09:50.526
WAKE UP
WEATHER REPORT BEGINS
KIRA LEAVES HOUSE
HAYATO MEETS ROHAN
LIGHTNING STRIKES PEPSI SIGN
EXPLOSION KILLS ROHAN KISHIBE

09:50.610 --> 09:52.028
JULY 16TH (FRI) 8:34 AM

09:54.989 --> 09:56.657
Hayato Kawajiri…

09:56.699 --> 09:58.826
What are you doing here?

09:58.993 --> 10:00.369
Was all this planned?

10:00.620 --> 10:03.873
Could this have something
to do with Rohan-sensei?

10:04.999 --> 10:09.253
<i>If they start questioning me
about Dad…</i>

10:09.337 --> 10:12.465
<i>There's no question… the bomb
will kill every one of them!</i>

10:14.050 --> 10:17.053
<i>N-No!
Don't ask me any questions…</i>

10:17.845 --> 10:22.099
<i>If you guys get killed,
then who's gonna kill him?</i>

10:23.017 --> 10:24.852
<i>If I have to dupe them,
then so be it…</i>

10:24.894 --> 10:28.397
<i>Whatever it takes…
I can't let them die!</i>

10:30.858 --> 10:32.943
I have something I'd like to
ask you about this photo…

10:34.028 --> 10:38.032
I'd like to know the reason
behind your video recording.

10:38.116 --> 10:40.409
Why were you taking video of you—

10:40.493 --> 10:42.536
Nosebleed!

10:42.578 --> 10:43.537
I have to go to the doctor!

10:43.579 --> 10:45.664
I-I don't know why
there's so much blood!

10:45.706 --> 10:47.249
Sorry… Gotta go!

10:47.291 --> 10:48.292
Hold it.

10:49.252 --> 10:52.546
You said you got a nosebleed,
let's see.

10:54.715 --> 10:56.299
Here. What happened?

10:58.469 --> 11:00.554
I have to go. I'm sorry.

11:00.596 --> 11:03.307
You don't have to see a doctor.

11:05.518 --> 11:07.269
Your nose isn't bleeding.

11:07.311 --> 11:08.103
Huh?

11:08.146 --> 11:09.605
Huh?!

11:11.732 --> 11:13.984
I'm Josuke Higashikata.

11:14.110 --> 11:17.071
And I'm related to that guy,
Jotaro Kujo.

11:17.113 --> 11:19.949
The guy with the dumb-ass grin
is Okuyasu Nijimura.

11:20.032 --> 11:21.491
And the face that shouts
world's nicest guy

11:21.576 --> 11:22.618
belongs to Koichi Hirose.

11:23.369 --> 11:25.871
You go to
Budogaoka Elementary, right?

11:25.913 --> 11:27.956
You still got some time
before classes start.

11:28.082 --> 11:29.917
We won't take much of your time…

11:30.251 --> 11:32.628
Now about this picture.

11:32.920 --> 11:35.964
If it's nothing,
we'll just be on our way.

11:36.215 --> 11:39.468
<i>It is something!
Just don't ask me any questions!</i>

11:39.802 --> 11:41.595
<i>You can't ask me any questions!</i>

11:41.721 --> 11:43.431
Is the person in this picture

11:44.765 --> 11:45.390
your da—

11:45.391 --> 11:48.644
No! Don't say any more!

11:52.398 --> 11:54.525
<i>So I guess that's it…</i>

11:54.734 --> 11:57.778
<i>Now they're going to ask
even more questions.</i>

11:58.946 --> 12:00.822
What do you mean
"Don't say anymore"?

12:00.907 --> 12:02.033
<i>They're all doing it now…</i>

12:02.116 --> 12:03.659
What shouldn't we say?

12:03.784 --> 12:05.035
<i>There's nothing I can do now!</i>

12:05.119 --> 12:07.079
Is this about your dad?

12:07.121 --> 12:08.330
<i>The bomb's gonna get them!</i>

12:08.581 --> 12:10.374
<i>It's gonna get them all!</i>

12:11.876 --> 12:13.419
You blurted out, "No!"

12:13.628 --> 12:15.463
"Don't say any more"?

12:15.505 --> 12:18.132
But we never even
asked you anything.

12:18.174 --> 12:19.383
I have a feeling…

12:19.467 --> 12:21.594
<i>- The bomb's gonna get them…</i>
- the mere act of questioning him

12:21.636 --> 12:24.013
<i>- The bomb… The bomb…</i>
- Is what's sending him into a panic.

12:24.764 --> 12:26.265
<i>That's it…</i>

12:29.352 --> 12:33.852
<i>I-If I die,
they'll still be able to live!</i>

12:34.732 --> 12:37.693
<i>I'm the bomb, I have to die!</i>

12:38.152 --> 12:39.361
<i>With me out of the picture,</i>

12:39.403 --> 12:43.903
<i>I know they'll defeat that devil
and save Mom!</i>

12:46.577 --> 12:51.077
Come on, let's just ask him
about Kosaku Kawajiri already.

12:51.999 --> 12:55.168
Wait, Josuke. Something's up.

12:56.504 --> 12:59.715
What's going on, what's wrong?

13:04.595 --> 13:06.388
<i>I can't do it…</i>

13:06.430 --> 13:09.391
<i>Something's keeping me
from slashing my throat!</i>

13:09.475 --> 13:10.225
That's…

13:10.309 --> 13:11.435
That Stand…

13:11.519 --> 13:13.812
I've never forgotten that face!

13:13.854 --> 13:15.230
Deadly Queen!

13:20.319 --> 13:21.194
Actually,

13:21.237 --> 13:24.990
you're looking at Deadly Queen's
bomb type three, Bites the Dust.

13:25.199 --> 13:26.909
To attack now would be futile.

13:26.993 --> 13:31.493
You see me now because I
have already entered your pupils.

13:32.623 --> 13:34.583
The number of you
is inconsequential,

13:34.667 --> 13:36.251
for in a single instant…

13:36.794 --> 13:40.214
Your folly was searching
for my true identity!

13:57.064 --> 13:59.691
What, you're already awake?

13:59.734 --> 14:02.528
I'm glad you finally
decided to answer me,

14:02.570 --> 14:05.197
but there's no need
to scream at me.

14:05.239 --> 14:07.449
Breakfast is ready,
come and get it.

14:14.081 --> 14:18.581
I couldn't stop him…
He got them too.

14:19.545 --> 14:23.590
It's all over now…
No matter what I do,

14:23.758 --> 14:28.258
in one hour, fate will wipe them
off the face of the earth…

14:29.805 --> 14:31.640
I can't even kill myself.

14:31.682 --> 14:33.642
My death would hinder his plan,

14:33.726 --> 14:37.813
so Bites the Dust is programmed
to protect me.

14:38.564 --> 14:40.148
He's unstoppable…

14:40.316 --> 14:43.110
Yoshikage Kira is
a horrible, horrible monster.

14:43.778 --> 14:45.237
Unless he dies

14:45.279 --> 14:49.366
or decides to shut off Bites
the Dust at exactly the right time,

14:49.450 --> 14:53.078
those guys are gonna die for sure.

15:09.178 --> 15:13.098
Unless he dies or shuts off Bites
the Dust at exactly the right time…

15:14.433 --> 15:18.933
<i>I never thought I could ever
be capable of killing a person.</i>

15:21.190 --> 15:25.690
<i>How could a puny 11-year-old kid
ever kill a monster like him…</i>

15:27.988 --> 15:30.240
<i>There is one way!</i>

15:30.324 --> 15:34.119
<i>An 11-year-old little punk
can kill him…</i>

15:34.245 --> 15:36.038
<i>…with one thing.</i>

15:37.665 --> 15:40.417
<i>I've got my own secret weapon</i>

15:40.501 --> 15:45.001
<i>slumbering in the shadows
of the attic.</i>

15:46.298 --> 15:48.216
<i>For the first time in my life,</i>

15:48.300 --> 15:51.594
<i>I found myself begging
and praying to God.</i>

15:52.346 --> 15:56.846
<i>Dear God, help me find
the strength to kill this man.</i>

16:09.113 --> 16:10.447
<i>So I was right.</i>

16:10.531 --> 16:14.076
<i>The sun makes this cat plant
spring to life,</i>

16:14.160 --> 16:16.620
<i>then it attacks by shooting
bullets of com pressed air.</i>

16:16.871 --> 16:20.624
<i>The power it can generate with
such little light is incredible.</i>

16:20.875 --> 16:22.042
<i>This killer instinct…</i>

16:22.084 --> 16:23.502
<i>I'll use its killer instinct,</i>

16:23.544 --> 16:26.922
<i>and send an air bullet
flying his way point blank.</i>

16:29.133 --> 16:30.676
<i>Pointblank…</i>

16:30.718 --> 16:33.220
<i>But when and how?</i>

16:34.013 --> 16:36.181
<i>I can't do it inside or nearby.</i>

16:36.515 --> 16:38.016
<i>Mom's here.</i>

16:39.852 --> 16:41.395
<i>That's it… My hat!</i>

16:41.437 --> 16:44.148
<i>He'll put that hat on my head.</i>

16:45.149 --> 16:47.151
<i>That'll be my chance!</i>

16:47.234 --> 16:50.237
<i>He'll come up right behind me,
right in point-blank range.</i>

16:50.362 --> 16:52.364
<i>That's when I'll get him!</i>

16:54.200 --> 16:57.119
<i>What? You're kidding!
We're already on air?</i>

16:57.328 --> 16:59.580
<i>Er, um… It's now 7:55…</i>

16:59.622 --> 17:02.833
Dad said he wanted
another cup of coffee.

17:08.923 --> 17:10.549
Hello?

17:11.217 --> 17:13.010
Nope, wrong number.

17:13.093 --> 17:15.553
This isn't the Sakurai residence.

17:24.271 --> 17:27.607
Sweetie, I have something special
here for you.

17:27.983 --> 17:30.777
A pipping hot cup of fresh coffee.

17:36.700 --> 17:38.201
Oh, that's right…

17:38.369 --> 17:39.870
What a pleasant morning.

17:39.954 --> 17:43.540
I suppose one more cup
before work wouldn't hurt.

17:44.041 --> 17:47.753
<i>Everything is set in stone under
Bites the Dust's power, right?</i>

17:48.128 --> 17:50.880
<i>Once something is broken,
it's destined to break again,</i>

17:50.965 --> 17:53.133
<i>and there's not a damn thing
I can do.</i>

17:53.634 --> 17:55.427
<i>You said it yourself</i>

17:59.598 --> 18:02.183
My favorite china tea set!

18:03.561 --> 18:04.687
<i>Take that ass!</i>

18:05.729 --> 18:08.982
All right, Mom, I'm off to school!

18:11.819 --> 18:13.570
<i>I'm looking out for you.</i>

18:13.654 --> 18:17.032
<i>I'll never let anyone
hurt you, Mom!</i>

18:29.086 --> 18:30.629
I'm in disbelief.

18:30.671 --> 18:35.171
I never have any idea what's
going on in that boy's head… But…

18:35.968 --> 18:39.513
Then there are days
he reminds me how much I love him.

18:39.680 --> 18:42.974
Oh, please don't. I can clean up.

18:43.517 --> 18:45.560
There's no use crying
over spilled milk.

18:45.644 --> 18:47.896
The important thing is that
you're okay, did it burn you?

18:47.980 --> 18:51.108
No… I'm perfectly fine.

18:57.698 --> 18:59.282
Still not here…

19:01.410 --> 19:04.496
H-He's not here…
He's nowhere to be seen.

19:06.790 --> 19:08.124
S-Something's off.

19:08.208 --> 19:09.918
Last time, he was already here
by this time…

19:10.085 --> 19:11.461
Why isn't he here?

19:11.545 --> 19:14.506
Darn, the weather report
never said anything about rain!

19:14.548 --> 19:16.508
I-It's starting to rain!

19:16.842 --> 19:21.342
<i>Did I change destiny
by leaving the house before him?</i>

19:21.722 --> 19:23.849
<i>No, that's impossible!</i>

19:23.891 --> 19:25.809
<i>As long as he tries to
put the hat on my head,</i>

19:25.893 --> 19:29.396
<i>there's no question
he'd approach me from behind.</i>

19:30.940 --> 19:33.901
L-Lightning struck the Pepsi sign!

19:34.109 --> 19:37.362
<i>Calm down. Relax!
I've still got two minutes!</i>

19:37.571 --> 19:40.156
<i>I have more than two minutes</i>

19:40.240 --> 19:42.325
<i>before Rohan Kishibe
spontaneously explodes.</i>

19:42.409 --> 19:43.660
<i>I just have to believe—</i>

19:48.499 --> 19:52.999
<i>In the shadows of the tree…
He's already here!</i>

19:54.505 --> 19:57.007
Under any other circumstance,
I'd say this is a pleasant morning.

19:57.091 --> 20:00.469
But Hayato wasn't himself…

20:00.511 --> 20:01.637
What's going on?

20:01.887 --> 20:04.055
It's just a feeling,
a strange feeling…

20:04.098 --> 20:07.309
We've relived this morning
several times now…

20:07.476 --> 20:10.645
Probably three,
no four times at least.

20:10.896 --> 20:13.648
Does he sense something's up?

20:13.899 --> 20:16.067
<i>It doesn't matter,
there's no time!</i>

20:16.110 --> 20:19.154
<i>I'll just have to blast him
from here.</i>

20:21.991 --> 20:25.369
Could he know
I'm holding the cat plant…

20:25.661 --> 20:28.330
Is that why
he's staying back there?

20:28.497 --> 20:31.333
No… If he knew,
he wouldn't be that close.

20:31.417 --> 20:35.917
I'll have to knock him off
with one shot.

20:36.130 --> 20:40.630
<i>If I miss, Rohan will explode,
his friends will be obliterated,</i>

20:41.635 --> 20:44.512
<i>and that murderer'll deactivate
Bites the Dust.</i>

20:44.555 --> 20:47.432
<i>If that happens,
he ends up the victor!</i>

20:47.474 --> 20:49.434
<i>There's no more time! Shit…</i>

20:49.476 --> 20:51.269
<i>Just one more step to the left!</i>

20:51.353 --> 20:54.481
<i>Just step out from the shadow
of that shitty tree</i>

20:54.523 --> 20:56.733
<i>so I can blow you away
to kingdom come!</i>

20:58.485 --> 21:01.905
<i>What?! H-He just hid himself
even more!</i>

21:01.989 --> 21:04.449
<i>The look in Hayato's eyes
this morning at the house…</i>

21:04.575 --> 21:06.952
<i>He radiated a certain tenacity
I've never seen before.</i>

21:07.161 --> 21:09.413
<i>The same look
that annoying Koichi Hirose</i>

21:09.496 --> 21:11.873
<i>and vile Josuke give off</i>

21:12.708 --> 21:16.753
<i>Something tells me
I need to watch his every move…</i>

21:17.129 --> 21:20.882
<i>Then again,
Hayato is completely helpless…</i>

21:20.924 --> 21:22.133
<i>Shit, I'm screwed!</i>

21:22.176 --> 21:24.553
<i>A few seconds past 8:29,</i>

21:24.636 --> 21:27.430
<i>and the bomb will start
ripping apart Rohan Kishibe!</i>

21:30.893 --> 21:33.061
<i>The brat is panic-stricken…</i>

21:33.145 --> 21:34.896
<i>like a desperate rat,</i>

21:34.938 --> 21:38.399
<i>toiling and drowning
in a cesspool of filth.</i>

21:38.817 --> 21:41.694
<i>I guess his tenacity was
just a figment of my imagination.</i>

21:42.029 --> 21:44.114
<i>Those are the eyes of
complete and utter defeat.</i>

21:45.074 --> 21:46.658
<i>So he finally came out!</i>

21:47.868 --> 21:51.538
<i>I came here to bring you
your hat, Hayato.</i>

21:53.540 --> 21:56.084
<i>If you're listening up there,
thank you, God.</i>

21:56.168 --> 21:58.086
<i>Thank you for
making that murderer</i>

21:58.170 --> 22:00.755
<i>leave the safety
of that tree's shadow!</i>

22:01.215 --> 22:03.133
<i>I'm ready to do this!</i>

22:03.425 --> 22:06.094
Suck on this, Yoshikage Kira!

22:12.559 --> 22:13.726
What?!

22:15.687 --> 22:17.188
I did it!

22:20.067 --> 22:23.111
A clean shot! I… I did it!

22:23.278 --> 22:25.822
Hayato Kawajiri's
nowhere to be seen…

22:25.906 --> 22:29.117
Perhaps he took
a different route to school.

22:33.455 --> 22:35.707
Prepare to die, murderer!

22:39.920 --> 22:43.173
W-W-What?!

22:44.550 --> 22:45.968
Lately…

22:46.051 --> 22:47.135
Impossible!

22:47.386 --> 22:50.097
My nails have exhibited
unprecedented growth…

22:50.556 --> 22:52.641
Which got me thinking
how lately my life

22:52.724 --> 22:55.268
has been devoid
of all that is good.

22:55.769 --> 22:57.437
But the contents of this pocket…

22:57.479 --> 22:59.189
confirm my feeling
that a guardian angel

22:59.273 --> 23:02.359
has returned to watch over me
from last night.

23:04.403 --> 23:08.240
Remember when I broke
Mom's special tea cup?

23:08.574 --> 23:12.369
The coffee spilled on my wrist,
giving me a nasty burn,

23:12.452 --> 23:13.870
so I took off the watch

23:13.954 --> 23:16.247
and placed it safe and sound
in my chest pocket.

23:16.290 --> 23:18.709
And Io and behold!

23:18.792 --> 23:22.378
Had I not spilled that coffee…

23:22.963 --> 23:27.175
<i>How… Howie that possible? I…</i>

23:27.593 --> 23:29.720
I… I blew it!

23:30.679 --> 23:34.432
That horrible moment
is almost here!

23:38.979 --> 23:42.023
EPISODE 37
SHINING D (DIAMOND)
IS UNBREAKABLE, PART 1
